But we need to refer to the parameter list; we cannot use \old(list) because list is a parameter, not changed. The condition "list is not null" is just list != null. So assert: list != null => (this.size() == list.size() && \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); this.get(i).equals(list.get(i)));

We need to use this.get(i).equals(list.get(i)) but list.get(i) is okay; list is an AttributeList, which has get method returning Attribute. That's public. So okay.

