analysisWe need to produce an assert statement for the comment in the constructor. The comment: "If the list is not null, then this list is equal to the provided list."

We need to express that if list != null, then this list equals list (i.e., contains same elements in same order). There is no explicit equals method defined, but we can use this.equals(list) perhaps. Since AttributeList extends ArrayList<Object>, equals is defined for lists (order-sensitive). So we can assert: list != null => this.equals(list). Use => syntax.

Thus final assert: assert list != null => this.equals(list);

Make sure syntax: <code>assert list != null => this.equals(list);</code>

